            "settings": {
              "body": "\"We had spalling on the north elevation within two winters of the previous treatment. Four years after switching, the same elevation is unchanged.\"\n\nThe difference is penetration depth. A surface film fails at the first freeze-thaw cycle that gets behind it; a penetrating treatment has nothing to lift.",
